+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "00dbb066-4da8-44d7-9cf6-9df6588e2d01",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "## Clustering fingerprints\n",
+    "\n",
+    "First to define an optimal threshold we will take a look into the average similarity of\n",
+    "the fingerprints we want to cluster. For this we will use the iSIM formalism which can\n",
+    "calculate the average similarity with linear complexity. You can notice how this value differs significantly from the one obtained in the other notebook where we use ECFP4 fingerprints."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 16,
+   "id": "cb054d6d",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Average similarity: 0.3177\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "isim = iSIM.jt_isim_packed(fps)\n",
+    "print(f\"Average similarity: {isim:.4f}\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "0566f24f",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Now, we will estimate the standard deviation of the similarities using a stratified\n",
+    "sample from our data set."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 17,
+   "id": "69a1a45b",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "Estimated std of similarity: 0.1029\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "isim_sigma = iSIM.estimate_jt_std(fps, n_samples=50)\n",
+    "print(f\"Estimated std of similarity: {isim_sigma:.4f}\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "83ff56f8",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "We have already identified that for most databases 3.5 or 4 isim sigmas over the global isim gives good clustering results."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 48,
+   "id": "8ea13ec3",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "text/plain": [
+       "BitBirch(threshold=0.6778597081973251, branching_factor=1024, merge_criterion='diameter')"
+      ]
+     },
+     "execution_count": 48,
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "execute_result"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "# Initialize the BitBirch tree. In general, diameter is the best merge criterion for\n",
+    "optimal_threshold = isim + 3.5 * isim_sigma\n",
+    "bb_tree = bblean.BitBirch(branching_factor = 1024, \n",
+    "                          threshold=optimal_threshold, \n",
+    "                          merge_criterion=\"diameter\")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# Cluster the packed fingerprints (By default all bblean functions take packed fingerprints)\n",
+    "bb_tree.fit(fps)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "5315dfa2-c3c6-41e6-ad43-57f19f16a28e",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Lets analyze the results to check the number of singletons"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 49,
+   "id": "7d746844-ff98-469b-83e8-ce5be5cfe4e7",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 300x400 with 1 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "clusters = bb_tree.get_cluster_mol_ids()\n",
+    "clusters_pop_plot(clusters)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 50,
+   "id": "c2758579",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 1250x625 with 2 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "# First we run a cluster analysis on the resulting ids\n",
+    "ca = analysis.cluster_analysis(clusters, fps, smiles, top = 10)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "# Afterwards we can use the utility functions on the bblean.plotting module\n",
+    "plotting.summary_plot(ca, title=\"Diameter\")\n",
+    "plt.show()"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "88318538",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "We can take a look at some of the structures to see if there they fit they make sense in terms of chemical structure."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 51,
+   "id": "8f431ecf",
