+   "source": [
+    "### Fingerprint comparison\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Here we will plot the pairwise similarities for carotenoid collection from obtained from COCONUT https://coconut.naturalproducts.net/collections?q= represted with ECFP4 and RDKIT fingerprints. We can notice how there is a difference of around 0.1 in the means, and how different the distributions are. Hence using the same threshold for both would not be ideal. \n",
+    "\n",
+    "Note that this step might take a while since we are doing pairwise comparisons depending on the database you test it with.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "We will download some smiles files first."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "3640ffbd",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "os.system(\"wget -q https://zenodo.org/records/17796465/files/chembl.smi\")\n",
+    "os.system(\"wget -q https://zenodo.org/records/17796482/files/carotenoids.smi\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 2,
+   "id": "18d744f7",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "smiles_carotenoids = bblean.load_smiles('carotenoids.smi')\n",
+    "fps = {}\n",
+    "sims = {}\n",
+    "for fp_type in ['ecfp4', 'rdkit', 'ap', 'topological']:\n",
+    "    fps[fp_type] = bblean.fps_from_smiles(smiles_carotenoids, fp_type, n_features=2048)\n",
+    "    sims[fp_type] = iSIM.jt_sim_matrix_packed(fps[fp_type])\n",
+    "\n",
+    "plot_distributions_by_fp(sims)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "efa51439",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Database comparison\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Now, let's compare how different the distributions are for two databases: the carotenoid we used in the first section and a random sample of the size from ChEMBL. We can see how even the difference is bigger; hence we cannot just use the same value for all databases."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 3,
+   "id": "f92b0e74",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "data": {
+      "image/png": "",
+      "text/plain": [
+       "<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>"
+      ]
+     },
+     "metadata": {},
+     "output_type": "display_data"
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "smiles_chembl = bblean.load_smiles('chembl.smi') #### Note: Download above file first\n",
+    "# Let's take a random sample of ChEMBL with the same size as the carotenoids dataset\n",
+    "smiles_chembl_sample = np.random.choice(smiles_chembl, size=len(smiles_carotenoids), replace=False)\n",
+    "chembl_sample_ecfp4 = bblean.fps_from_smiles(smiles_chembl_sample, 'ecfp4', n_features=2048)\n",
+    "ecfp4_sims = {'carotenoids': sims['ecfp4'],\n",
+    "              'chembl_sample': iSIM.jt_sim_matrix_packed(chembl_sample_ecfp4)}\n",
+    "\n",
+    "plot_distributions_by_fp(ecfp4_sims)"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "173880ec",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Selecting the optimal threshold\n",
+    "\n",
+    "iSIM which is linear scaling way of calculating the average of the pairwise similarities without having to compute them. With iSIM, we can quickly obtain the average and use it as reference to select our threshold. \n",
+    "\n",
+    "For instance, for the two databases above:\n"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 4,
+   "id": "db094e22",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [],
+   "source": [
+    "# Let's get now the complete fingerprints for ChEMBL\n",
+    "chembl_ecfp4 = bblean.fps_from_smiles(smiles_chembl, kind = 'ecfp4')"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": 6,
+   "id": "f96ea0a7",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "iSIM Carotenoids ECFP4: 0.2496\n",
+      "iSIM ChEMBL ECFP4: 0.1126\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "# Calculating iSIM for both databases\n",
+    "iSIM_carotenoids = iSIM.jt_isim(fps['ecfp4'])\n",
+    "iSIM_chembl = iSIM.jt_isim(chembl_ecfp4)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(f\"iSIM Carotenoids ECFP4: {iSIM_carotenoids:.4f}\")\n",
+    "print(f\"iSIM ChEMBL ECFP4: {iSIM_chembl:.4f}\")"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "a013f321",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "We can see that in the distribution of ECFP4 fingerprints using typical values of what would be consider \"similar\" (e.g., 0.70), would not give the best results. BitBirch uses as merging criterion the iSIM of a subcluster, hence using a value that much larger than the average (e.g., 0.11 for ChEMBL) would give an extremely large number of singletons. \n",
+    "\n",
+    "We are going to use the standard deviation of the similarities to guide the threshold selection. But we won't have to calculate all the pairwise similarities, for the estimation of the standard deviation we will use iSIM-sigma, an efficient linear scaling aproach.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "The differences in standard deviations are also significant."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "code",
+   "execution_count": null,
+   "id": "1ae633eb",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "outputs": [
+    {
+     "name": "stdout",
+     "output_type": "stream",
+     "text": [
+      "iSIM-sigma Carotenoids ECFP4: 0.1260\n",
+      "iSIM-sigma ChEMBL ECFP4: 0.0378\n"
+     ]
+    }
+   ],
+   "source": [
+    "iSIM_sigma_carotenoids = iSIM.estimate_jt_std(fps['ecfp4'])\n",
+    "iSIM_sigma_chembl = iSIM.estimate_jt_std(chembl_ecfp4)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "print(f\"iSIM-sigma Carotenoids ECFP4: {iSIM_sigma_carotenoids:.4f}\")\n",
+    "print(f\"iSIM-sigma ChEMBL ECFP4: {iSIM_sigma_chembl:.4f}\") # Rsults may vary due to this estimation not being deterministic"
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "1df6ec79",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "Takeaway:\n",
+    "- The distribution of similarities can highly differ between fingeprint types and databases. \n",
+    "- iSIM and iSIM-sigma can be used as reference to define a threshold for each case."
+   ]
+  },
+  {
+   "cell_type": "markdown",
+   "id": "586e3ce9",
+   "metadata": {},
+   "source": [
+    "### Cluster with informed thresholds\n",
+    "\n",
+    "We now are going to test several thresholds in increasing standard deviation steps. For full calculations please use the `optimal_threshold.py` script contained in this directory. That script might take a while to run, since it tests several thresholds until 1.0\n",
